WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:04.610
Episode 2 of "House of the Dragon" revolves
around the Hightowers and their efforts to

00:00:04.610 --> 00:00:10.130
convince Princess Rhaenyra that her father,
King Viserys, should remarry. and choose the

00:00:10.130 --> 00:00:15.340
teenage Alicent Hightower over the 12-year-old
Laena Velaryon, who's the better candidate

00:00:15.340 --> 00:00:16.340
on paper.

00:00:16.340 --> 00:00:20.770
Rhaenyra and her father have barely spoken
since her mother and brother's traumatic deaths,

00:00:20.770 --> 00:00:25.470
so Alicent takes the princess to the Sept
to pray … but this scene means much more

00:00:25.470 --> 00:00:26.580
than you might think.

00:00:26.580 --> 00:00:30.820
The Hightowers are the lords of Oldtown, where
they were once the richest and most powerful

00:00:30.820 --> 00:00:32.349
family in Westeros.

00:00:32.349 --> 00:00:36.670
The Faith of the Seven — the predominant
religion in Westeros — has strong ties there

00:00:36.670 --> 00:00:37.670
as well.

00:00:37.670 --> 00:00:41.510
The Hightowers support the Faith, while the
Targaryens … not so much.

00:00:41.510 --> 00:00:45.609
Publicly, they've converted, but they keep
to their ancient customs and try to limit

00:00:45.609 --> 00:00:46.690
the Seven's reach.

00:00:46.690 --> 00:00:51.270
By getting Rhaenyra to bend the knee in prayer,
Alicent is flexing her own strength.

